================================================================================================
READING IT
================================================================================================
  PART 1 must be monotone decreasing: attenuation only ever loses signal.
  A fitted d far from M means the ansatz does not carry degree-M content,
  which is itself worth knowing - (*) says the attenuation base reports
  the EFFECTIVE degree, not the parameter count.

  PART 2 is the test. If the empirical argmax sits at the predicted R*,
  the radius becomes a computed quantity and the sweep is redundant. If
  the argmax sits near 0.60 instead, the SNR derivation does not govern
  what the tuned value was selected for, and 0.6 stays a fitted constant
  - in which case the honest statement is that V6 still has one knob
  with no theory behind it.
